00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.959
buttons feel like real buttons it's kind

00:00:00.969 --> 00:00:02.430
of something you have to experience in

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.319
order to really understand now the

00:00:04.329 --> 00:00:05.819
benefit of touch response is that you

00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:07.979
really have to click in on a button in

00:00:07.989 --> 00:00:09.360
order to get it to register as a

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.889
physical click like you would with a

00:00:10.899 --> 00:00:13.109
physical button and if you graze an icon

00:00:13.119 --> 00:00:14.760
you don't necessarily go into that

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.530
portion of the menu that's good because

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.030
when you're driving you don't get false

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.620
positives as you're sort of bumping

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:21.300
along the road but if you prefer a

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:22.710
lighter touch you can turn off touch

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.780
response in a menu now along the edge

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.490
closest to the driver you have five

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.770
shortcuts that are customizable and they

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.510
are pretty much consistent they'll be

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:31.830
here no matter where you go in the

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.210
interface if you pop into the map

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.649
they'll be there if you go into the

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:36.960
radio they'll be there as well the rest

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.730
of the interface uses large icons that

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.440
are very easy to click and one of the

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:41.789
things that I really like about the

00:00:41.799 --> 00:00:43.800
system is that it's customizable if you

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.300
don't like the order that things are in

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.000
you can touch and hold and then just
